  "name": null,
  "problem": "Let $S$ be the set of all $2\\times 2$ matrices with real entries and determinant $1.$ Which of the following statements are true?  \n\nI. The identity matrix $[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]$ belongs to $S.$\n\nII. For any $A\\in S,$ we can find the corresponding negative matrix $-A\\in S$ such that $A+(-A)=O.$\n\nIII. There are matrices $A,B,C\\in S,$ such that $(A+B)+C\\ne A+(B+C).$",
